{"subtitleNullable":"Per year statistics for professional outdoor lacrosse players across two leagues","creatorNameNullable":"TJ Mulderig","totalBytesNullable":136440,"licenseNameNullable":"CC0: Public Domain","descriptionNullable":"### Context\n\nThe Premiere Lacrosse League (PLL) is entering its third season and has seen continued growth since inauguration. Data-driven insights, now common place in popular sports, could be a large benefit for coaches of the league and those involved in sports betting or fantasy lacrosse leagues. I will use this data to draw insights and hopefully win my fantasy lacrosse league. I hope others can find some use out of this data as well.\n\n### Content\n\nThese data sets contain per year statistics for every player in the 2019 MLL, 2020 MLL, 2019 PLL, 2020 PLL, 2021 seasons. \n\n**General legend:**\nplayer_name - Player\u0027s name\t\nteamId - Team player was on\t\ngamesPlayed - number of games player\t\npoints - sum of goals, two point goals, and assists\t\ntotalGoals - sum quantity of goals and two point goals as opposed to point sum\ntwoPointGoals - goals scored from two-point arc that count as two goals, worth two points\t\npowerPlayGoals - goals scored on power play\t\nshortHandedGoals - goals scored while other team is on power play\t power play\npim\t- penalty minutes\nSOFF - shots off goal, either regular or two-point shots\t\nSOGpct - shots on goal percent\nstatLeague - League player was in at the time PLL or MLL\t\nseasonSegment - either regular season or post season\t\n\n### Acknowledgements\n\nI\u0027d like to acknowledge and thank Jake Watts of the PLL for providing these statistics. ","ownerNameNullable":"TJ Mulderig","ownerRefNullable":"tjmulderig","titleNullable":"Professional Lacrosse Statistics (PLL \u0026 MLL)","currentVersionNumberNullable":5,"usabilityRatingNullable":0.8235294,"thumbnailImageUrlNullable":"https://storage.googleapis.com/kaggle-datasets-images/1387590/2301214/de212e4d9b8f253127acac0cfcb1fbb3/dataset-thumbnail.jpg?t=2021-06-04-02-08-47","id":1387590,"ref":"tjmulderig/professional-lacrosse-statistics-pll-mll","subtitle":"Per year statistics for professional outdoor lacrosse players across two leagues","hasSubtitle":true,"creatorName":"TJ Mulderig","hasCreatorName":true,"creatorUrl":"","hasCreatorUrl":false,"totalBytes":136440,"hasTotalBytes":true,"url":"","hasUrl":false,"lastUpdated":"2022-04-02T19:49:27.61Z","downloadCount":412,"isPrivate":false,"isFeatured":false,"licenseName":"CC0: Public Domain","hasLicenseName":true,"description":"### Context\n\nThe Premiere Lacrosse League (PLL) is entering its third season and has seen continued growth since inauguration. Data-driven insights, now common place in popular sports, could be a large benefit for coaches of the league and those involved in sports betting or fantasy lacrosse leagues. I will use this data to draw insights and hopefully win my fantasy lacrosse league. I hope others can find some use out of this data as well.\n\n### Content\n\nThese data sets contain per year statistics for every player in the 2019 MLL, 2020 MLL, 2019 PLL, 2020 PLL, 2021 seasons. \n\n**General legend:**\nplayer_name - Player\u0027s name\t\nteamId - Team player was on\t\ngamesPlayed - number of games player\t\npoints - sum of goals, two point goals, and assists\t\ntotalGoals - sum quantity of goals and two point goals as opposed to point sum\ntwoPointGoals - goals scored from two-point arc that count as two goals, worth two points\t\npowerPlayGoals - goals scored on power play\t\nshortHandedGoals - goals scored while other team is on power play\t power play\npim\t- penalty minutes\nSOFF - shots off goal, either regular or two-point shots\t\nSOGpct - shots on goal percent\nstatLeague - League player was in at the time PLL or MLL\t\nseasonSegment - either regular season or post season\t\n\n### Acknowledgements\n\nI\u0027d like to acknowledge and thank Jake Watts of the PLL for providing these statistics. ","hasDescription":true,"owne